  "scientific_diagnosis": "The accuracy drop at small random noise (L2 ~ 0.01) is NOT a pipeline artifact (raw perturbed and pipeline-constrained perturbations produce identical curves). It is an inherent structural property of axis-aligned decision trees trained on IoT network telemetry: over 20-35% of network flows sit exactly on constant mass points (e.g., flow_duration = 0, Variance = 0). Because decision trees place sharp step thresholds directly adjacent to these mass points (over 45,000 splits within 0.05 of flow_duration = -0.0662), even tiny isotropic random perturbations of magnitude 0.01 push thousands of samples across leaf decision boundaries simultaneously."
